Package: baggingReserve
Title: Bagging and Regression Trees for Individual Claims Reserving
Version: 0.1.1
Authors@R: c(
    person("Jan", "Janoušek", email = "janousek@karlin.mff.cuni.cz",
           role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0007-3731-4416")),
    person("Michal", "Pešta", email = "pesta@karlin.mff.cuni.cz", role = "aut",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-5311-0797")))
Description: Individual (claim-by-claim) loss reserving in non-life insurance with
    regression trees and bootstrap aggregating (bagging), as proposed by Janoušek
    and Pešta (2025) <doi:10.1007/s00362-025-01715-9>. One regression tree is
    calibrated per development year and the lower triangle of outstanding
    payments of reported claims is filled recursively one development year ahead;
    bagging yields replicate reserve predictions whose spread describes the
    resampling variation of single-tree predictions, and the out-of-bag score
    serves as a diagnostic of the one-year regressions. Payments for
    incurred-but-not-reported claims are predicted from chain-ladder claim counts
    and the average predicted payment per development year. Ships a reproducible
    synthetic individual-claims dataset generated with 'SynthETIC'.
